{"title":"What should I ask Alexander Mikaberidze?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/973208408/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Alexander-Mikaberidze.html","date":1794943045000,"content":"<p>He is the author and the new and excellent <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Louisiana-Purchase-Bargain-America-American/dp/0197548148/ref=sr_1_3?crid=3FWOUW8M52258&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.-sRADA4WYIhWjVkeUVGFeZE6W5ktABKDA_jdgurhuFeY3Ypm5W5fBBC1NW0ymWszlXBB36_t4dZSodfGfilmZZ4xwYJ8-EUHT_erbbX_2yZIguwS3Z75RwrmHp-ckx8RXzCn1U84HPYn4g5SKX4JWXlpt7jkNIcYKM1Jmg7p8vYEsNr7upJBQ3clxb2FhMLg83OCBbsnoNSONo12mo8cyxRrZkvhDpK1EZEcLymD_i23nk_lx-SfrJcfl8IXjoy2y_86G_qlio4n2Jxg7B-6cxpDA5j_uUyptzDYyAgNkXw.80rRy6ZT4D-12jmUgD7RhNmop7FMUdxk7gPmLCcMtuQ&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=louisiana+purchase&amp;qid=1794852867&amp;sprefix=louisiana+purc%2Caps%2C485&amp;sr=8-3\" target=\"_blank\">The Louisiana Purchase: The Grand Bargain and the Making of America</a>.  He also wrote <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Napoleonic-Wars-Global-History/dp/0199951063/ref=tmm_hrd_swatch_0\" target=\"_blank\">The Napoleonic Wars: A Global History</a>, one of my favorite history books.  He has extensive other writings on the history of the Russian military during that same period.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Mikaberidze\" target=\"_blank\">From Wikipedia</a>:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p><b>Alexander Mikaberidze</b> (<a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian_language\">Georgian</a>: <span><span>ალექსანდრე მიქაბერიძე</span></span>; born 27 January 1978) is a <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgia_(country)\">Georgian</a> lawyer, author and historian who specializes in <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleonic_studies\">Napoleonic studies</a>. He is a full professor of history and social sciences at <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_State_University_in_Shreveport\">Louisiana State University in Shreveport</a>, where he holds the Ruth Herring Noel Endowed Chair for the Curatorship of the James Smith Noel Collection, one of the largest private collections of antiquarian books, prints, and maps in the United States. In 2025, he was granted the Boyd Professorship, the highest and most prestigious academic rank awarded by Louisiana State University.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>He is a scholar and historian in the very best old-fashioned sense of the term, one of the most underrated writers and scholars today.  So what should I ask him?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/11/what-should-i-ask-alexander-mikaberidze.html\">What should I ask Alexander Mikaberidze?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/973208408/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/973208408/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/973208408/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/973208408/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/973208408/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feed